      strings
      file
      objdump
      xxd
      hexdump
      binwalk
      exiftool
      Ghidra
      hexedit
      gdb
      pwndbg
      strace
      checksec
      javap
      javac
      JD-GUI
      UPX
      

START
 |
 |--[1] Initial triage
 |      |
 |      |-- What file type is it?
 |           |
 |           |-- ELF (Linux)
 |           |-- PE (.exe Windows)
 |           |-- Mach-O (macOS)
 |           |-- Script (Python, JS, etc.)
 |
 |      |-- Run basic checks:
 |           - file
 |           - strings
 |           - checksec
 |           - ldd (Linux)
 |
 |--[2] Can you run it?
 |      |
 |      |-- YES --> Execute safely
 |      |          |
 |      |          |-- Observe:
 |      |               - input prompts
 |      |               - output messages
 |      |               - crashes
 |      |               - flag format hints
 |      |
 |      |-- NO --> Static-only path
 |
 |--[3] Quick wins (ALWAYS DO THIS)
 |      |
 |      |-- strings output contains:
 |           |
 |           |-- "flag", "CTF", "key", "pass" ?
 |           |-- suspicious base64/hex blobs?
 |           |-- URLs / file paths?
 |           |
 |           |-- YES --> decode/analyze immediately
 |
 |--[4] Packing / obfuscation?
 |      |
 |      |-- Signs:
 |           - very few strings
 |           - weird section names
 |           - high entropy
 |
 |      |-- YES --> unpack first:
 |           - UPX → `upx -d`
 |           - manual unpack via debugger
 |
 |--[5] Static analysis
 |      |
 |      |-- Load into:
 |           - Ghidra / IDA / Binary Ninja
 |
 |      |-- Find:
 |           - main()
 |           - entry point
 |
 |      |-- Identify:
 |           |
 |           |-- Input handling?
 |           |-- strcmp / memcmp?
 |           |-- loops / conditions?
 |           |-- crypto routines?
 |           |-- encoding logic?
 |
 |--[6] Input validation branch
 |      |
 |      |-- Program asks for input?
 |           |
 |           |-- YES -->
 |                |
 |                |-- Locate checks:
 |                     - strcmp
 |                     - hash comparison
 |                     - arithmetic checks
 |
 |                |-- Then:
 |                     |
 |                     |-- Simple compare?
 |                     |      --> Extract correct string
 |                     |
 |                     |-- Transformed input?
 |                     |      --> Reverse the transformation
 |                     |
 |                     |-- Complex constraints?
 |                            --> Use Z3 / symbolic execution
 |
 |--[7] Encoding / encryption branch
 |      |
 |      |-- Detect patterns:
 |           |
 |           |-- XOR?
 |           |-- Base64?
 |           |-- ROT?
 |           |-- custom loops?
 |
 |      |-- Strategy:
 |           |
 |           |-- Reimplement logic in Python
 |           |-- Reverse operations step-by-step
 |
 |--[8] Control flow complexity
 |      |
 |      |-- Many branches / conditions?
 |           |
 |           |-- YES -->
 |                |
 |                |-- Patch binary:
 |                     - bypass checks
 |                     - force success path
 |                |
 |                |-- OR dynamic analysis
 |
 |--[9] Dynamic analysis branch
 |      |
 |      |-- Use debugger:
 |           - gdb / pwndbg
 |           - x64dbg (Windows)
 |
 |      |-- Breakpoints:
 |           |
 |           |-- main
 |           |-- strcmp / memcmp
 |           |-- exit
 |
 |      |-- Inspect:
 |           - registers
 |           - stack
 |           - memory
 |
 |      |-- Trick:
 |           |
 |           |-- Stop at comparison
 |           |-- Read expected value directly
 |
 |--[10] Anti-debug / tricks?
 |       |
 |       |-- Detect:
 |            - ptrace
 |            - timing checks
 |            - weird crashes
 |
 |       |-- Bypass:
 |            - patch instructions
 |            - nop checks
 |
 |--[11] Advanced path
 |       |
 |       |-- Obfuscated logic?
 |            |
 |            |-- Use:
 |                 - symbolic execution (angr)
 |                 - emulation
 |
 |--[12] Flag retrieval
 |       |
 |       |-- Found directly in:
 |            - strings
 |            - memory dump
 |            - decoded blob
 |
 |       |-- OR:
 |            |
 |            |-- Correct input → program prints flag
 |            |
 |            |-- OR patched binary reveals flag
 |
 END
